{"schema_version":3,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:39-2","provision":"BCO 39-2","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"39-2","title":"Section 39-2","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/39-2/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/39-2","current_text":{"html":"<p>When the proceedings of a lower court are before a higher court, the members of the lower court shall not lose the right to sit, deliberate and vote in the higher court, except in cases of appeal or complaint.</p>","text":"When the proceedings of a lower court are before a higher court, the members of the lower court shall not lose the right to sit, deliberate and vote in the higher court, except in cases of appeal or complaint."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"3215b08b64db0d1ab36e0721b999ec192d812d74","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"e5fd669690c4b80754c46f09d04273adf2ccbfb6563342677c52c5cde8a91808","assessment_fingerprint":"517b100d2e9006e313ab6d84d4f0f31593b77832f395383ba2227779470cd034","assessment_summary":{"status":"stale","file":"index/provision_link_adjudications.jsonl","total":11481,"expected":12455,"applied":0,"stale":11481,"unmatched":0,"unassessed":12455},"parent_id":"bco:39","children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recommendations":{"status":"incomplete","note":"Recommendation and study papers are not comprehensively indexed by provision."},"history":"partial"},"relationship_count":12,"relationships":[{"id":"bco:39-2--inquiry:inquiries/ga12_1984__ci05.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga12_1984__ci05.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Scope and duration of BCO debate prohibitions during a complaint","year":1984,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci05.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci05.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:39-2--inquiry:inquiries/ga12_1984__ci05.md:occ-862b5c4b6e7c","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci05.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga12_1984__ci05.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/inquiries_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga12_1984__ci05.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"summary":"BCO prohibitions on debate apply only to the specific matter complained, only until final adjudication, and to all members of the lower court — expiring upon final resolution."}},{"id":"bco:39-2--case:cases/ga52_2025__2023-21.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga52_2025__2023-21.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Kang et al. v. Korean Central Presbytery","year":2025,"disposition":"not_sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga52_2025__2023-21.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga52_2025__2023-21.md","evidence_basis":"multiple","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:39-2--case:cases/ga52_2025__2023-21.md:occ-89c2ad627522","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga52_2025__2023-21.html","repository_path":"cases/ga52_2025__2023-21.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga52_2025__2023-21.md"},{"id":"bco:39-2--case:cases/ga52_2025__2023-21.md:occ-ff82baf55c32","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga52_2025__2023-21.html","repository_path":"cases/ga52_2025__2023-21.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"matters of discretion and judgment (BCO 39-2(3)). Judgments and decisions","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga52_2025__2023-21.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"case_numbers":["2023-21"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Three Teaching Elders complained that Korean Central Presbytery clearly erred in declining to indict a Teaching Elder after a BCO 31-2 investigation into allegations of financial impropriety, spiritual abuse, and physical abuse. The SJC held that KCP did not clearly err, given the age of the allegations and the…"}},{"id":"bco:39-2--case:cases/ga44_2016__2015-03.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga44_2016__2015-03.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Flesher and Weekly v. Metro Atlanta Presbytery","year":2016,"disposition":"dismissed","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga44_2016__2015-03.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga44_2016__2015-03.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:39-2--case:cases/ga44_2016__2015-03.md:occ-4111ed859ddd","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga44_2016__2015-03.html","repository_path":"cases/ga44_2016__2015-03.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga44_2016__2015-03.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["moot","complaint adjudicated in related appeal"],"standard_of_review":"not_reached","case_numbers":["2015-3"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"In Complaint 2015-03, Steve Flesher and Randy Weekly challenged Metro Atlanta Presbytery, but the SJC did not reach the merits. Because the issues raised had already been adjudicated in Appeal 2015-08, the SJC declared Complaint 2015-03 moot and approved that disposition. The short decision thus records a mootness ruling based on prior appellate adjudication; the underlying presbytery action and the Appeal 2015-08 decision are not described in the supplied text."}},{"id":"bco:39-2--case:cases/ga44_2016__2015-08.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga44_2016__2015-08.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Hardie v. Metro Atlanta Presbytery","year":2016,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga44_2016__2015-08.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga44_2016__2015-08.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:39-2--case:cases/ga44_2016__2015-08.md:occ-f654ad4a286c","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga44_2016__2015-08.html","repository_path":"cases/ga44_2016__2015-08.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":94},"excerpt":"The standard of review for this Court is set forth in BCO 39-2 and 3:","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga44_2016__2015-08.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["appeal denied","indefinite suspension","ordination vows","judicial commission procedure","indictment","BCO 31-2 investigation","BCO 31-10 suspension without censure","hearsay evidence","witness qualification","BCO 31-8 malignant spirit","BCO 39-2 standard of review","clear error standard"],"standard_of_review":"mixed","review_standards":["factual_findings","discretion_and_judgment"],"case_numbers":["2015-8"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"TE John Hardie appealed his Metro Atlanta Presbytery conviction on three charges of breaking ordination vows and indefinite suspension, alleging seventeen procedural and evidentiary errors. Applying BCO 39-2/3 clear-error deference, the SJC denied every specification and upheld the judgment and censure. It found no clear error in the BCO 31-2 investigation, indictment/prosecutor process, commission membership, evidence rulings, scheduling, alleged prejudice, or censure. It assessed transcription costs equally while encouraging MAP to absorb them, and cautioned that an absent commissioner's vote might support a future challenge."}},{"id":"bco:39-2--case:cases/ga41_2013__2012-05.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga41_2013__2012-05.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Hedman v. Pacific Northwest Presbytery","year":2013,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga41_2013__2012-05.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga41_2013__2012-05.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:39-2--case:cases/ga41_2013__2012-05.md:occ-a215095e3cee","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga41_2013__2012-05.html","repository_path":"cases/ga41_2013__2012-05.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":98},"excerpt":"- **e.** BCO 39-2.4 “[A] higher court should not consider itself obliged to exhibit the same deference to a lower court when the issues being reviewed involve the interpretation of the Constitution of the Church.\"","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga41_2013__2012-05.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["Federal Vision","Westminster Standards","Peter Leithart","baptism","covenant of works","imputation","justification","union with Christ","not guilty","standard of review","deference to lower court","standing","complaint vs. appeal","Federal Vision theology","sacraments"],"standard_of_review":"mixed","review_standards":["factual_findings","discretion_and_judgment"],"case_numbers":["2012-5"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"The SJC denied RE Gerald Hedman's complaint against Pacific Northwest Presbytery, which had adopted five not-guilty judgments on charges that TE Peter Leithart's baptism, covenant, imputation, justification, and union-with-Christ views contradicted the Westminster Standards. Bound to the record and clear-error review, the SJC found no procedural violation and insufficient evidence that Presbytery clearly erred. It left the verdicts undisturbed, declined to endorse Leithart's views generally, and urged continued clarification of his non-standard terminology. A separate dissent would have found error and ordered a new trial or reference."}},{"id":"bco:39-2--case:cases/ga40_2012__2011-13.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga40_2012__2011-13.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Spann v. Oak Mountain Presbyterian Church","year":2012,"disposition":"dismissed","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga40_2012__2011-13.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga40_2012__2011-13.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:39-2--case:cases/ga40_2012__2011-13.md:occ-d1a5cf257134","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga40_2012__2011-13.html","repository_path":"cases/ga40_2012__2011-13.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga40_2012__2011-13.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["premature appeal","excommunication without process","appeal to next higher court","spiritual abuse","OMSJC 2.10"],"standard_of_review":"not_reached","case_numbers":["2011-13"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"An individual appealed directly to the SJC, alleging her church effectively excommunicated her without process, failed the Matthew 18 process, and spiritually abused her by social isolation. The SJC dismissed as premature, without reaching the merits, because there was no record of a judicial decision by the church or of an appeal to Evangel Presbytery, the next higher court; it stated she could proceed only by providing such evidence. The severity of excommunication did not excuse that prerequisite. The SJC asked Presbytery to obtain the session's written response to her letter."}},{"id":"bco:39-2--case:cases/ga36_2008__2007-08.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga36_2008__2007-08.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Jones v. Louisiana","year":2008,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga36_2008__2007-08.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga36_2008__2007-08.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:39-2--case:cases/ga36_2008__2007-08.md:occ-e6645ddab88e","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga36_2008__2007-08.html","repository_path":"cases/ga36_2008__2007-08.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":172},"excerpt":"in this case. The issues in this case do not involve issues of fact (BCO 39-2)","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga36_2008__2007-08.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["constitutional_interpretation","differences_with_standards","westminster_standards","election","perseverance","apostasy","visible_invisible_church","baptism","presbytery_procedures","federal_vision","judicial_review","church_discipline"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2007-8"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Louisiana Presbytery’s refusal to institute process after examining Steve Wilkins’s Federal Vision teachings was challenged for applying the wrong constitutional standard and overlooking a strong presumption that some views were out of conformity with the Westminster Standards. The SJC sustained the complaint and annulled Presbytery’s denial. A “difference” need not expressly contradict the Standards; Presbytery must independently investigate and classify it rather than accept the member’s assurance or shift the burden to objectors. The ruling did not adjudicate Wilkins’s guilt; the Central Carolina memorial remained before the SJC."}},{"id":"bco:39-2--case:cases/ga33_2005__2003-02_2003-05.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga33_2005__2003-02_2003-05.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Thornton v. Westminster","year":2005,"disposition":"sustained_in_part","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga33_2005__2003-02_2003-05.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga33_2005__2003-02_2003-05.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:39-2--case:cases/ga33_2005__2003-02_2003-05.md:occ-2fc7ada3609d","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga33_2005__2003-02_2003-05.html","repository_path":"cases/ga33_2005__2003-02_2003-05.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":218},"excerpt":"acquaintance of the events and parties.\" (BCO 39-2.3)","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga33_2005__2003-02_2003-05.md"},{"id":"bco:39-2--case:cases/ga33_2005__2003-02_2003-05.md:occ-fc7e3720f243","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga33_2005__2003-02_2003-05.html","repository_path":"cases/ga33_2005__2003-02_2003-05.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":218},"excerpt":"acquaintance of the events and parties.\" (BCO 39-2.3)","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga33_2005__2003-02_2003-05.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["secret taping","phone recording","investigation procedure","prosecutorial authority","voluntary prosecutor","partiality","judicial process","deference to lower courts"],"case_numbers":["2003-5"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Westminster Presbytery was found to have erred in its BCO 31-2 investigation of secret taping by TE Frank Smith by failing to obtain full witness testimony and investigate legal ramifications; case remanded. The court found no proof of partiality and declined to require establishment of unbiblical criteria for secret taping. Vote: 18 concurring, 1 dissenting (RE Frederick Neikirk), 2 recused, 1 abstained, 2 absent."}},{"id":"bco:39-2--case:cases/ga26_1998__1997-05.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga26_1998__1997-05.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Mt. Carmel Session v. New Jersey Presbytery","year":1998,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga26_1998__1997-05.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga26_1998__1997-05.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:39-2--case:cases/ga26_1998__1997-05.md:occ-dc7dc0ec76b7","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga26_1998__1997-05.html","repository_path":"cases/ga26_1998__1997-05.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga26_1998__1997-05.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["creation days","days of Genesis One","24-hour day interpretation","Westminster Confession WCF IV:1","in the space of six days","presbytery authority to resolve questions of doctrine","BCO 11-4 doctrinal questions","affirmations and denials","minority report","confessional subscription","age-day creation","hermeneutics"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["1997-5"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Mt. Carmel Session challenged New Jersey Presbytery's creation-days resolution, arguing that the Westminster Standards require six consecutive twenty-four-hour days. The SJC majority concluded that Presbytery could resolve the doctrinal question under BCO 11-4 and that prior Assembly actions permitted latitude on the length of the creation days. The General Assembly rejected the minority report, adopted the majority report, and denied the complaint."}},{"id":"bco:39-2--rpr_exception:rpr/exc/ohio__022.html","record_id":"rpr_exception:rpr/exc/ohio__022.html","type":"RPR exception","title":"Ohio: The members of the lower court were permitted to sit, deliberate, and vote on complaint ag","year":2025,"disposition":"raised","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/rpr/exc/ohio__022.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/rpr/exc/ohio__022.html","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:39-2--rpr_exception:rpr/exc/ohio__022.html:occ-67009fc8250f","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/rpr/exc/ohio__022.html","repository_path":"rpr/exc/ohio__022.html","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["index/rpr_search.json:provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/rpr/exc/ohio__022.html"}],"reference_presenta